- [ES client creation and TCC/entitlement requirements](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_new_client(_:_:))
- [Apple-requested ES entitlement](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.developer.endpoint-security.client)
- [Global sequence counter and version requirement](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_message_t/global_seq_num)
- [Per-event sequence counter and drops](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_message_t/seq_num)
- [Process identities and audit tokens](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_process_t)
- [NOTIFY_FORK](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_event_type_notify_fork), [AUTH_EXEC](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_event_type_auth_exec)
- [Launch environment constraints and XPC responsibility](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Security/applying-launch-environment-and-library-constraints)
- [Apple launchd source manual: AbandonProcessGroup](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/launchd/blob/main/man/launchd.plist.5)
- [Client destruction errors](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/endpointsecurity/es_delete_client(_:))

These sources support OS mechanisms and their boundaries; none attests this candidate
was built, run, entitled, installed, connected or capable of complete native containment.
